# Scratch artifacts at repo root. `_*` is the repo's convention for local
# scratch (captures, probes, logs, one-off generators) and it is deliberately
# extension-agnostic. This block used to enumerate extensions
# (`/_*.png`, `/_*.log`, `/_*.json`, `/_*.txt`) and the list fell behind:
# `/_*.py` and `/_*.xml` were never added, so `_gen_wf.py`, `_wf_gen.py`,
# `_r2_a11y_guard.py`, `_r3_palette_probe.py` and `_p12_junit.xml` were
# tracked (REL-M1). A rule that enumerates extensions is a rule that goes
# stale; guard: tests/test_repo_hygiene.py.
/_*

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

